From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:47:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ci(js-tests): probe temp-dir fsync and cgroup PSI during
 workspace checks (#335)

* ci(js-tests): probe temp-dir fsync and cgroup PSI during workspace checks

Main run 41087044980 failed on four tests that each froze 24-34 s while the
same sha passed twice; total test time was equal across runs. The summary now
says whether the disk, memory reclaim or CPU stalled.

* ci(js-tests): probe temp-dir fsync and cgroup PSI during workspace checks

Main run 41087044980 failed on four tests that each froze 24-34 s while the
same sha passed twice; total test time was equal across runs. The summary now
says whether the disk, memory reclaim or CPU stalled.

* fix(ci): isolate disposable JS fixtures from overlay fsync stalls

* fix(ci): detach busy temporary mounts and retain backing-disk probe

* ci(js): fall back to /dev/shm when the runner denies tmpfs mount

* ci(js): keep fixture roots short enough for Unix sockets
